<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Waterford</h1><p class="st-meta">914 CE – 1170 CE (approx.) · capital Waterford</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Norse town-kingdom at the mouth of the Suir, often called Ireland's oldest city, until its storming by the Anglo-Normans in 1170.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> raided the south-east in the 9th century, and in 914 a large fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragnall-ua-imair">Ragnall</a> established a base at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a>, Vedrafjordr. The settlement grew into a fortified trading town ruled by Norse kings or jarls, sometimes linked to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-dublin">Kingdom of Dublin</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a> traded wine, slaves and goods across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-sea">Irish Sea</a> and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Its rulers became Christian and accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> consecrated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canterbury">Canterbury</a> from 1096. Irish overkings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-munster">Munster</a>, especially the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obrien-dynasty">O'Briens</a>, often controlled the town, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reginalds-tower">Reginald's Tower</a> recalls its Norse defences.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1170 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-fitzgerald">Raymond le Gros</a> stormed the town, and Strongbow married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aoife-macmurrough">Aoife</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a>, there. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II</a> landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waterford">Waterford</a> in 1171 and made it a royal city in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-ireland">Lordship of Ireland</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 914 CE – 1170 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:77.89%;width:5.09%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>914 CE – 1170 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Waterford</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ragnall ua Imair</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Norse paganism; Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Norse, Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vedrafjordr, Norse Waterford</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1042&amp;focus=kingdom-of-waterford" aria-label="Kingdom of Waterford on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4520 373 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Waterford lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4840 629L4823 622M4840 629L4861 599"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4823 622h0M4861 599h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4840 629h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4840 629h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Waterford. <a href="/atlas?year=1042&amp;focus=kingdom-of-waterford">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

